        "title": "Planetary Interiors and Magnetic Fields",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "We cannot drill to the core of any planet (except partially Earth). Everything we know about planetary interiors comes from indirect probes: seismology, gravity fields, magnetic fields, moment of inertia, and heat flow. Planetary magnetism comes from convective dynamos in electrically conducting fluid layers."
